{"entryId":"2816","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:2816:1","sourceSha256":"bfd5b6e22921df961e24343a3daaebd0f18723fc6faf81fce98dd37783cc3cb9","englishSha256":"0cb0de5a5d028212215a193641ee90f6ad97f20f5cbad050a8738ad5daf6ca70","citations":[{"id":"2816:1:link-01","he":[7,20],"en":[10,19],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_13b.24"},"reference":"Sotah 13b:24","assessment":"Semalyon’s utterance concerns Moses’s death. The passage itself gives no identification as sage or angel.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sotah 13b:24","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_13b.24"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sifrei Devarim 357:28","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sifrei_Devarim_357.28"},"witness":"Sefaria Vocalized Edition"}]},{"id":"2816:1:link-02","he":[21,34],"en":[21,49],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Sotah_13b.24.2"},"reference":"Rashi on Sotah 13b:24:2","assessment":"The Rashi gloss explicitly has the sage interpretation.","evidence":[{"reference":"Rashi on Sotah 13b:24:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Sotah_13b.24.2"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"2816:1:link-03","he":[35,54],"en":[51,117],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sefer_HeArukh%2C_Letter_Samekh_225"},"reference":"Sefer HeArukh, Letter Samekh 225","assessment":"The cited entry of the Arukh includes both readings, leading with sage and giving angel as an alternative. Heilprin quotes only the latter, which the translation can retain and qualify.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sefer HeArukh, Letter Samekh 225","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sefer_HeArukh%2C_Letter_Samekh_225"},"witness":"Sefer HeArukh, Lublin 1883"}]},{"id":"2816:1:link-04","he":[55,79],"en":[119,153],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Sotah_13b.24.1"},"reference":"Tosafot on Sotah 13b:24:1","assessment":"Tosafot explicitly reports both, mentioning R. Ḥananel and Arukh in this short gloss.","evi